 you both  thanks for your time this evening let's  start then shall we with uh the latest  on the ukraine situation and moyer the  front of the daily telegraph  quoting president biden we will respond  in kind if putin uses chemicals very  clever  use of wording there was a lot of  ambiguity we don't quite know what the  red lines are  but it's still a bold statement  well yes i mean bison was responding to  a question put directly to him which  said would you use chemical weapons if  putin used them so the only thing he  could really do to avoid escalation is  to use that vague language i think  frankly um he was at an emergency summit  in brussels of nato and g7 members where  they were discussing the current  response to events in ukraine what's  really interesting about this is  what we've seen and i think also your  correspondent uh touched upon this just  before the break is that the war in  ukraine is not going the way russia  thought it had um they thought it'd be  very very quickly instead we've seen a  concerted and determined response from  ukraine and in fact now people are  starting to say hang on a minute maybe  maybe russia won't win this at all  and and the questions are rising as to  russia in a desperate position what will  they do next  uh yeah i mean annabelle it certainly um  did show didn't it today uh just how  unified western leaders are nato really  never more united than it was today and  putin in fact getting the very opposite  of what he was intending  well yes of course just weeks ago he was  hoping and quite  succeeding really in stoking division  between  nato members if you can remember back uh  that far there was disagreement over the  sorts of sanctions that they would be  willing to impose particularly germany  reluctant to  cease north stream too which is now  subsequently done it's increased defense  spending so you're absolutely right that  there's a lot more unity among nato  members um  my concern is how vladimir putin is  going to respond to all of this i  thought before he sent tanks into  ukraine that he was a rational political  actor my worry now is that he's going to  think well  better to be hung for a sheep than for a  lamb you know is this sort of tough uh  if ambiguous rhetoric  really going to stop him particularly as  maya says when he appears to be on the  back foot the past four weeks have put  paid to the idea that ukraine would uh  swiftly capitulate or keeve would uh  even welcome uh russian soldiers russian  tanks this war is quite clearly not  going as putin planned um it's still not  clear how far  the west is willing to go the western  alliance is willing to go in this but  they've i think already gone further  than i was expecting  let's stay with ukraine but but a  different angle front page of the metro  kiss it  bye  jet setter daughter of an oligarch has  her assets frozen um tell us a bit about  this moya  so yeah this is uh the glamorous paulina  colova  she is the daughter of svetlana  pollakova who happens to be the  unofficial wife of sergey lavrov who is  a very high-ranking minister defence  minister in putin's administration and  she is now one of the latest  people with the connections to russia to  have her assets frozen so she is also  prohibited from traveling to or from the  uk and much has been made of polina i  think because her life is very  documented on instagram she's young  she's glamorous she's somebody that  people can sort of seize onto as an  example of what happens when these  sanctions are applied in real time um  but what is quite interesting is she  represents the international russian  elite the people who  well of the west is hoping will put  pressure upon putin um the more these  sanctions are applied to them there was  an interesting report in the times  yesterday suggesting if the war and  sanctions drag on uh top fsb officials  are already starting to  murmur just murmur about turning on  putin because they're very angry at the